-- same-text: the pieces of text held by more than one module. A module is the list of its pieces'
-- hashes, and a hash is its text's, so one hash in two modules is one text in two places: the same
-- declaration by content, with nothing to prove before one copy is kept. A line is the piece's hash, a
-- tab, the module.
hy-sx-some : List Word → Bool
hy-sx-some nil = false
hy-sx-some (cons c r) = if %weq c #9 then false else true
